:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="changelog-overlay">
		<div class="changelog-hero">
			<span class="changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.21.2</span></h1>
				<div class="changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Updated RBE to v0.6.1.2</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Bags now have their own slot</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Purses, messenger bags, gym bags, tote bags, luggage, the vintage suitcase, and backpacks now use a dedicated <strong>Bag</strong> slot instead of the Handheld slot.</li>
		<li>Bags can now be worn while also holding umbrellas, parasols, canes, fishing rods, or other Handheld items.</li>
		<li>Shops now have a <strong>Bag</strong> tab and wardrobes have a <strong>Bag</strong> row.</li>
		<li>Scenes that temporarily remove carried items now take and return both Bag and Handheld items correctly.</li>
		<li>The POCKET bag tab still follows the equipped bag.</li>
		<li>The foraging basket remains a Handheld item.</li>
		<li>Bag artwork is unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Scarves now have their own slot</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Scarves, fur boas, holy stoles, and neck cushions now use a dedicated <strong>Scarf</strong> slot instead of the Neck slot.</li>
		<li>Scarves can now be worn together with collars or necklaces.</li>
		<li>Shops now have a <strong>Scarf</strong> tab and wardrobes have a <strong>Scarf</strong> row.</li>
		<li>Existing scarves automatically move to the new slot when loading a save, including worn, carried, stored, dropped, Bailey-confiscated, and outfit-saved items.</li>
		<li>Scenes that remove or return neckwear still handle scarves correctly.</li>
		<li>Scarf artwork is unchanged and draws over collars.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added the Magical Menagerie</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added buyable pets by <strong>Grimace</strong> and <strong>Zerolefox</strong>.</li>
		<li>Pets can live in the player's room, get hungry or bored, build Bond, leave if neglected, and be found again later.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Snakes</strong>, bought from the pet shop and requiring a terrarium and suitable food.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Slimes</strong>, which are harder and more expensive to obtain and require discovering the cabin by the lake first.</li>
		<li>Slimes feed on suitable things produced by the player's body instead of normal food.</li>
		<li>Feeding and playing with pets raises Bond.</li>
		<li>Pets can be carried outside: snakes ride on the neck and slimes sit on the head, with both appearing on the player sprite (vanilla only atm).</li>
		<li>Pets only accept appropriate food and may refuse or become sick from the wrong food.</li>
		<li>High-Bond pets can defend the player during encounters.</li>
		<li>Snakes strike enemies, while slimes slap enemies and absorb some Pain.</li>
		<li>Pet attacks become stronger with Bond and do not count as attacks made by the player.</li>
		<li>Low-Bond pets may run away instead.</li>
		<li>Pets may interfere even during consensual encounters, with NPC reactions to their involvement.</li>
		<li>Lost pets can later be found in the forest, at the lake, or in Garter's back room depending on how they disappeared.</li>
		<li>Bond slowly falls while a pet is away, but the pet still remembers the player.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>X-Change Fame now has reputation titles</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added X-Change Fame titles ranging from <strong>Pill Popper</strong> to <strong>The Many-Faced</strong>.</li>
		<li>X-Change Fame can combine with other Fame types for mixed titles such as <strong>Kindly Stranger</strong>, <strong>Two-Faced Dealer</strong>, <strong>Social Chameleon</strong>, and <strong>Dual Cover Star</strong>.</li>
		<li>Higher Fame levels unlock stronger title variants.</li>
		<li>Maxing all relevant Fame can unlock <strong>The One and Only, Twice Over</strong>.</li>
		<li>Mixed titles now check actual Fame thresholds correctly.</li>
		<li>If no mixed title qualifies, the strongest normal reputation is shown instead.</li>
		<li>The X-Change Fame meter in the Social menu now uses the correct scale.</li>
		<li>Fixed Mickey saying “Hello again, (title)” during the first meeting.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded recipes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Gwylan can teach <strong>Wolfbrew</strong> and <strong>Ghostbrew</strong> through a 15-minute shop interaction after relationship stage 1.</li>
		<li>Both brews can also be learned from the cookbook after easier recipes.</li>
		<li>Wolfshrooms and Ghostshrooms can replace normal mushrooms using the existing ingredient controls.</li>
		<li>Added substitutions for fish, cloudberries, mushrooms, and Water Dragon eggs.</li>
		<li>Wolfbrew and Ghostbrew cannot be given as NPC gifts or donated to the soup kitchen.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated audio</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added unique music for Poppy instead of using the Sea background track.</li>
		<li>Added ambient weather audio for rain, thunder, and similar conditions.</li>
		<li>Ambient audio is muffled indoors.</li>
		<li>Setting the ambience volume to 0 disables it.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Improved clothing-slot migration</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Clothes moved between slots are now converted on every type of load before other clothing systems run.</li>
		<li>Coats and bags are found wherever they are stored: worn, carried, in any wardrobe, left somewhere, confiscated by Bailey, or saved in an outfit.</li>
		<li>This fixes the previous jacket/vest conversion only checking the orphanage wardrobe.</li>
		<li>Existing coats or bags already lost in an older version cannot be recovered; use a save from before the affected update if available.</li>
		<li>Bags can once again be destroyed by scenes.</li>
		<li>Bags no longer create tan lines.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Bailey rent collection</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Bailey now uses the player's <strong>rent deposit first</strong>, then <strong>savings</strong>, then <strong>cash</strong> when collecting rent in person.</li>
		<li>This applies at the orphanage, temple, farm cottage, Poppy's flat, and on the street.</li>
		<li>If the deposit fully covers rent, Bailey takes it and leaves without showing a payment prompt.</li>
		<li>Offering yourself as payment also uses the rent deposit first.</li>
		<li>Payment checks now include the brat tax when determining affordability.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Avery's saved pill route</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Avery no longer automatically becomes angry simply because the player returns home unpilled.</li>
		<li>After saving Avery, returning unpilled now follows Avery's normal Rage instead.</li>
		<li>At low Rage, Avery gives a warning and gains only a small amount of Rage.</li>
		<li>Repeatedly returning unpilled can still eventually trigger the chase once Rage is high enough.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Premium X-Change pills</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added <strong>Beta (second womb)</strong> to the Premium side-effect list beside Alpha.</li>
		<li>Beta can now be selected directly instead of being limited to random spikes or cheats.</li>
		<li>Choosing Beta alongside <strong>Make body female</strong> or <strong>Make body herm</strong> now correctly grants Beta when starting from a male body.</li>
		<li>Premium pills now allow effect-only choices during pregnancy or parasite broods while body swaps remain blocked.</li>
		<li>Effect-only Gray pills remain usable.</li>
		<li>Gray pills with the optional sex-swap setting still obey pregnancy restrictions.</li>
		<li>Effect-only sessions grant +340 Beauty without stacking, including Premium pills.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Autism stimming</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Removed misplaced Stim links from Gameplay Settings passages.</li>
		<li>Affected areas include Asylum, Eden Cabin, Wolf Cave, Livestock, Pirate, Prison, Temple, Water Dragon Lab, and Nest.</li>
		<li>Added Stim spots to the <strong>Meadow</strong> and <strong>Coast</strong>.</li>
		<li>Meadow and Coast count as quiet/private places, so stimming there gives full Load relief.</li>
		<li>If another NPC is actually present, the reduced social version is used instead.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated skill-status tooltips</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Skill-status tooltips have been revised to make their meaning clearer.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added advanced blusher option</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added <strong>Skip desaturate filter</strong> to the advanced blusher colour-picker panel under <strong>Waterproof</strong>.</li>
		<li>Reverted the previous blusher layering tweak.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed Kylar pronouns</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed ear-slime orgasm handling</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Breeder/Omega denial no longer accidentally triggers the Ear Slime orgasm reward.</li>
		<li>Ear Slime now has its own marker.</li>
		<li>Only an actual Ear Slime ruined orgasm gives the Ear Slime text, -1 Trauma, and +1 Corruption.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed escape digging</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Digging out of the farm, wolf cave, and underground cell no longer becomes excessively slow when injured or exhausted.</li>
		<li>Poor condition can reduce digging speed only to half speed at worst.</li>
		<li>Miniature bodies can correctly squeeze out of the farm barn and underground cell.</li>
		<li>Farm field and barn scenes now recognise completed escape tunnels.</li>
		<li>The wolf cave no longer announces the exit before the tunnel is actually finished.</li>
		<li>The underground cell no longer allows escape before enough digging has been completed.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Whitney's park-public-sex ending</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The untie line now appears only when the player's arms are actually bound.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed hair dye</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Hairdresser dye colours no longer all display as the same red swatch.</li>
		<li>Dye selection no longer assigns invalid hair colours that can cause <code>canvasfilter</code> errors in the mirror.</li>
		<li>Saves with broken hair colours are repaired on load.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Sirris's parasite chastity removal</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Robin's drink stand</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed class hallway events always appearing late</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed baby descriptions</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Corrected parentage flags.</li>
		<li>Fixed Great Hawk paternity checks.</li>
		<li>Generated NPC descriptions are now preserved after birth.</li>
		<li>Existing children recover parentage information from saved records when viewed.</li>
		<li>If an old save already lost the mother's description, it now displays <strong>A stranger</strong> instead of <code>pregnancy_#</code>.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed BGM recovery</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>BGM no longer remains permanently silent after interrupted or failed playback.</li>
		<li>Audio retries on the next update without restarting music that is already playing.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Renamed Refrigenerator to Refrigerator</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Ivory Wraith possession</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Wraith possession now initialises Resistance correctly.</li>
		<li>Affected saves are repaired on load.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gwylan's clothing requests</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Gwylan now avoids clothing blocked by hypnosis settings.</li>
		<li>Existing impossible requests can be exchanged for ingredients.</li>
		<li>Hypnotic Crossdressing now follows the current setting correctly.</li>
		<li>Fixed related wardrobe and shop checks.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Tentacle encounters</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Wraith marks can now correctly reduce encounters to one tentacle.</li>
		<li>Sea Vore checks whether the right arm is available before restraining it and updates narration accordingly.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed prison jumpsuit initialisation</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The prison jumpsuit now initialises correctly when entering prison.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon images" aria-hidden="true">&#10024;</span> Art and Graphics</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Added vanilla Modded Face 11</strong> by <strong>snowy</strong>.
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added vanilla Modded Face 12</strong> by <strong>noufi</strong>.
		</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
<</widget>>
